LIB_LOAD("pq",{"p2c1":{"challenge":[{"q":"Who brought Christiana the King's letter?","o":["Secret","Evangelist","Great-heart","Mercy"],"why":"A messenger named Secret."},{"q":"What were the names of Christiana's four sons?","o":["Matthew, Samuel, Joseph and James","Peter, John, Paul and Luke","Simple, Sloth, Presumption and Pliable","Faithful, Hopeful, Honest and Great-heart"],"why":"Matthew, Samuel, Joseph and James."},{"q":"Why did Mercy worry about coming?","o":["She had no invitation letter","She was too young","She couldn't walk","She was afraid of Christiana"],"why":"Christiana promised to ask for her, and kept her promise."},{"q":"Whose daughter was Mrs Timorous?","o":["Timorous, who ran from the lions","Obstinate","Giant Despair","Evangelist"],"why":"Fear ran in the family."},{"q":"What did the Keeper say to Mercy when she fainted?","o":["\"Damsel, I bid thee arise\"","\"Go home\"","\"Wait outside\"","\"Who are you?\""],"why":"He lifted her up himself."},{"q":"Why was there a barking dog near the gate?","o":["The enemy kept it there to frighten pilgrims","To guard the Keeper","It was a pet","It was lost"],"why":"Fear is one of the enemy's favourite tools."},{"q":"Why didn't the women have protection on the road?","o":["They didn't ask the Keeper for a guide","Great-heart was sick","They wanted to be alone","Reliever refused"],"why":"They thought the danger was small."},{"q":"The man with the muck-rake never...","o":["Looked up","Stopped eating","Went outside","Said thank you"],"why":"He missed the crown above his head."},{"q":"What does the robin that eats spiders teach?","o":["Some people look good outside but have bad habits inside","Birds are beautiful","Spiders are food","Always feed birds"],"why":"Looking good and being good are not the same."},{"q":"Complete: \"Set your affection on things above, not on things on the ___.\"","o":["earth","table","ground","road"],"why":"Colossians 3:2. Look up!"}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Which famous Part I traveller was Christiana's husband?","o":["Christian","Faithful","Hopeful","Evangelist"],"why":"Now his whole family is on the road!"},"choices":[{"title":"Bring someone along","q":"Your cousin just moved to your school. Every break time, he sits alone while your group plays football.","o":[{"t":"Invite him to join your group, and introduce him to everyone.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Christiana didn't go alone. She brought Mercy along."},{"t":"Wave at him, but leave him be.","f":"A wave is nice, but an invitation changes everything."},{"t":"Wait for a teacher to sort it out.","f":"Leaders don't wait for someone else to notice. They act."}]},{"title":"Speak up for a friend","q":"You've been picked for the school quiz team. Your friend, who is just as good, wasn't even told about the trials.","o":[{"t":"Ask the teacher if your friend can still try out.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Christiana at the gate: \"Please let my friend in too.\""},{"t":"Keep quiet. You're already in.","f":"Christiana got in, and then she knocked for Mercy."},{"t":"Tell your friend it's not fair, and complain about the teacher.","f":"Complaining doesn't open gates. Asking kindly does."}]},{"title":"Ask for a guide","q":"You're leading five juniors home from an evening church programme. They want to take a dark shortcut through a bush path.","o":[{"t":"Take the main road, and ask an adult to walk with you.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Christiana learned it the hard way: ask for a guide before trouble comes."},{"t":"Take the shortcut. You'll be quick.","f":"That's how the women met the two rough men. Don't underestimate danger."},{"t":"Let the juniors decide.","f":"When you're the leader, you're responsible for their safety."}]},{"title":"The muck-rake","q":"Your youth group is offering a free weekend leadership training. You'd rather spend the weekend on your phone, scrolling and gaming.","o":[{"t":"Put the phone down, sign up, and grow.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Look up! There's a crown being offered."},{"t":"Stay on your phone. There will be other trainings.","f":"That's the muck-rake: looking down while the crown waits above you."},{"t":"Sign up but scroll through the whole training.","f":"Showing up isn't the same as looking up."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"road","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Part II, Chapter 1 in real life."},{"sc":"home","n":"🫂 Bring someone along. Every journey is better when you invite someone who is standing alone."},{"sc":"gate","n":"🗣️ Speak up for others. Use your voice for the people who are left outside the gate."},{"sc":"road","n":"🛡️ Ask for help early. Before trips, events or new challenges, ask: what could go wrong, and who can help?"},{"sc":"muckrake","n":"👆 Look up. Don't spend your life raking up things that don't last."}],"stops":{"p2c1s1":{"story":[{"sc":"home","n":"Back in the City of Destruction, {Christiana} hears the news: her husband Christian has crossed the river. He is safe in the Celestial City."},{"sc":"home","w":"christiana","e":"worried","t":"I laughed at him. I called him crazy. I made it hard for him to go. And now he's gone, and I'm still here with my sins."},{"sc":"home","n":"Her four sons, Matthew, Samuel, Joseph and James, cry with her. They remember how their father begged them to come along."},{"sc":"night","n":"That night, Christiana dreams. She sees Christian in a place of joy, standing near the King, with a harp in his hand."},{"sc":"home","n":"Next morning, someone knocks. A visitor named {Secret} comes in."},{"sc":"home","w":"secret","e":"smile","t":"Christiana, the Merciful One sent me to tell you: He is ready to forgive. And He invites you to His house."},{"sc":"home","n":"Secret gives her a letter. It smells of the finest perfume, and it's written in gold. The King invites her to come the same way Christian went."},{"sc":"home","w":"christiana","e":"big","t":"My sweet boys, let's go! Let's follow your father to the Celestial City!"},{"sc":"home","w":"matthew","e":"big","t":"Yes, Mum! Let's go!"},{"sc":"city","n":"Just then, two neighbours arrive: {Mrs Timorous}, and a kind young woman named {Mercy}."},{"sc":"city","w":"mrstimorous","e":"shock","t":"Christiana! Have you lost your mind? Don't you remember what happened to your husband? The swamp, the lions, Apollyon? Stay home!"},{"sc":"city","w":"christiana","e":"smile","t":"I'm going. And Mercy, will you come with me?"},{"sc":"city","w":"mercy","e":"worried","t":"I'd love to. But I didn't get a letter. Will the King want me too?"},{"sc":"city","w":"christiana","e":"big","t":"Come with me. I'll ask for you at the gate. The King said there is room for everyone who comes!"},{"sc":"road","n":"Mrs Timorous goes home to gossip. And Christiana, her four boys and Mercy set out on the road."}],"quote":{"text":"Christiana, the Merciful One hath sent me to tell thee that He is a God ready to forgive.","who":"Secret"},"lesson":{"title":"Turn around, then bring others","text":"Christiana once mocked the journey. When she changed her mind, she didn't go alone. She brought her children, and she invited Mercy, even though Mercy had no letter. Leaders don't just start the journey; they look around and ask, \"Who can I bring with me?\""},"think":"Is there someone who might come along if you simply invited them: to church, to a club, to a study group?","quiz":[{"q":"What news did Christiana hear about Christian?","o":["He was safe in the Celestial City","He was lost in the swamp","He had come home","He was in Doubting Castle"],"why":"Christian had crossed the river and reached the Celestial City."},{"q":"How did Christiana feel about how she treated Christian?","o":["Sorry, because she had mocked him and made it hard for him","Proud of herself","Happy he left","She didn't care"],"why":"She was sorry, and that sorrow turned her around."},{"q":"What did Secret bring her?","o":["A letter from the King, written in gold","A bag of money","A sword","A map of the city"],"why":"A personal invitation from the King."},{"q":"Why was Mercy worried about coming?","o":["She had not received a letter","She was scared of dogs","She was too old","She had no shoes"],"why":"But Christiana promised to ask for her at the gate."},{"q":"How did Mrs Timorous react?","o":["She tried to scare Christiana into staying home","She joined them","She gave them food","She cried with joy"],"why":"Like her father Timorous, she let fear do the talking."}]},"p2c1s2":{"story":[{"sc":"swamp","n":"Soon they reach the Slough of Despond, the swamp where Christian sank. It's still muddy and slippery."},{"sc":"swamp","w":"mercy","e":"worried","t":"Come, let's be brave, but let's be careful."},{"sc":"swamp","n":"This time they look for the steps. They walk slowly, one by one. Christiana nearly slips once or twice... but they all get across!"},{"sc":"swamp","n":"As they come out, they hear a voice: \"Blessed is she that believed: for there shall be a performance of those things which were told her from the Lord.\""},{"sc":"gate","n":"At last they reach the Wicket Gate. Christiana knocks. Nobody answers."},{"sc":"gate","n":"She knocks again. Suddenly a big dog starts barking loudly from the other side! The women and the boys freeze with fear."},{"sc":"gate","w":"christiana","e":"worried","t":"What do we do? If we go back, the Keeper may be offended. If we knock again, the dog might attack us."},{"sc":"gate","n":"They decide to knock again, louder than ever."},{"sc":"gate","w":"keeper","e":"stern","t":"Who is there?"},{"sc":"gate","w":"christiana","e":"worried","t":"Please don't be offended that we knocked at your royal gate. I am Christiana, Christian's wife. These are his sons. We've come the way he came."},{"sc":"gate","w":"keeper","e":"big","t":"Welcome! Come in, all of you!"},{"sc":"gate","n":"But Mercy is still outside, alone. She is so afraid of being turned away that she knocks hard... and faints right there."},{"sc":"gate","w":"christiana","e":"worried","t":"My Lord, my friend Mercy is outside. She wasn't invited like me, but she wants to come so much. Please let her in!"},{"sc":"gate","n":"The Keeper opens the gate. Mercy is lying on the ground. He takes her gently by the hand."},{"sc":"gate","w":"keeper","e":"smile","t":"Damsel, I bid thee arise.","b":true},{"sc":"gate","w":"mercy","e":"worried","t":"I came for something I was never invited to. Is there room for me?"},{"sc":"gate","w":"keeper","e":"smile","t":"I pray for everyone who believes in me, no matter how they come to me. Come in!"},{"sc":"gate","n":"Then the Keeper explains the dog. It belongs to {Beelzebub}, the enemy who lives in the castle nearby. He keeps it there to frighten pilgrims away from the gate."}],"quote":{"text":"Damsel, I bid thee arise.","who":"Keeper"},"lesson":{"title":"Speak up for others","text":"Christiana got in, but she didn't forget her friend outside. She asked the Keeper to let Mercy in too. And when Mercy fainted with fear, the Keeper lifted her up himself. Leaders use their voice for people who feel left out, and they lift up the ones who are afraid."},"think":"Is there someone 'outside the gate' at your school, someone left out, that you could speak up for?","quiz":[{"q":"How did Christiana's group cross the Slough of Despond?","o":["Slowly and carefully, looking for the steps","They swam","They jumped over it","Help carried them"],"why":"They learned from Christian's story and looked for the steps."},{"q":"What frightened them at the gate?","o":["A big dog barking","A lion","A storm","A giant"],"why":"The enemy's dog, put there to scare pilgrims away."},{"q":"What did Christiana do when the dog barked?","o":["Knocked again, even louder","Ran home","Threw a stone at the dog","Waited all night"],"why":"She kept knocking. Fear didn't stop her."},{"q":"What did Christiana do for Mercy?","o":["Asked the Keeper to let her in","Told her to go home","Left her outside","Gave her a letter"],"why":"Leaders speak up for people who are left outside."},{"q":"Who owned the barking dog?","o":["Beelzebub, the enemy","The Keeper","Mrs Timorous","Great-heart"],"why":"The enemy uses fear to keep people away from the gate."}]},"p2c1s3":{"story":[{"sc":"orchard","n":"Inside the gate, the road runs beside a high wall. On the other side is a garden. Its fruit trees hang right over the wall."},{"sc":"orchard","n":"The fruit looks delicious. The boys pick some and start eating."},{"sc":"orchard","w":"christiana","e":"stern","t":"Boys! That's not ours. Don't eat it!"},{"sc":"orchard","w":"james","e":"big","t":"But Mum, it's just hanging there!"},{"sc":"orchard","n":"They don't know that the garden belongs to the enemy. They'll find out later that this fruit is not good for them."},{"sc":"road","n":"A little further on, two rough-looking men come towards them. They block the road and try to grab Christiana and Mercy!"},{"sc":"road","w":"christiana","e":"shock","t":"Stay back! Leave us alone!"},{"sc":"road","n":"The women scream and fight back, shouting for help. And help comes! A man runs from the direction of the gate. His name is {Reliever}."},{"sc":"road","n":"The two men see him coming, jump over the wall, and run away into the enemy's garden."},{"sc":"road","w":"reliever","e":"stern","t":"Are you all right? I was surprised. When the Keeper let you in, why didn't you ask him for a guide to protect you?"},{"sc":"road","w":"christiana","e":"worried","t":"We didn't think we needed one. We thought the danger was small."},{"sc":"road","w":"reliever","e":"smile","t":"It's always good to ask for help before you need it. Go on, and stay alert."},{"sc":"road","w":"mercy","e":"worried","t":"We were so happy about getting in that we forgot to think about the danger ahead."}],"quote":{"text":"I marvelled much when you were entertained at the gate, that ye petitioned not the Lord for a conductor.","who":"Reliever"},"lesson":{"title":"Know your weak spots, and ask for help early","text":"The boys grabbed fruit that wasn't theirs. The women walked on without protection because they thought the danger was small. Leaders who look after others think ahead. They ask for help BEFORE trouble comes, and they don't let excitement make them careless."},"think":"When you're in charge of younger children, what dangers should you think about ahead of time?","quiz":[{"q":"Where did the fruit the boys ate come from?","o":["The enemy's garden, over the wall","The Interpreter's garden","A market","Their home"],"why":"It looked good, but it belonged to the enemy."},{"q":"What did Christiana tell the boys?","o":["Not to eat it, because it wasn't theirs","To pick more","To share it","To hide it"],"why":"She warned them, but they didn't listen."},{"q":"Who rescued the women from the two rough men?","o":["Reliever","Great-heart","Evangelist","Mr Honest"],"why":"Reliever came running from the gate."},{"q":"What had they forgotten to ask the Keeper for?","o":["A guide to protect them","Food","A map","Money"],"why":"They thought the danger was small. It wasn't."},{"q":"What is the main lesson from this stop?","o":["Ask for help before trouble comes","Always eat what you find","Walk faster","Never travel with friends"],"why":"Leaders think ahead for the people they look after."}]},"p2c1s4":{"story":[{"sc":"house","n":"They arrive at the Interpreter's house. The Interpreter has heard all about Christian, and he welcomes Christiana and her family with joy."},{"sc":"muckrake","n":"He takes them into a room. A man is there, looking only at the floor. He holds a {muck-rake} and keeps raking up straw, sticks and dust."},{"sc":"muckrake","n":"Above his head stands someone holding a shining crown, offering it to him in exchange for the muck-rake. But the man never looks up. He just keeps raking dirt."},{"sc":"muckrake","w":"christiana","e":"worried","t":"I think I know what this means. This is a person who only cares about the things of this world.","b":true},{"sc":"muckrake","w":"christiana","e":"worried","t":"Oh, deliver me from this muck-rake!"},{"sc":"house","n":"Next he shows them the very best room in the house. \"What do you see?\" Mercy looks hard. \"Nothing.\" Then Christiana spots it: a big spider on the wall."},{"sc":"house","w":"interpreter","e":"smile","t":"\"The spider taketh hold with her hands, and is in kings' palaces.\" Even an ugly spider can be in the King's best room. However bad you feel you are, faith can bring you into the King's house."},{"sc":"farm","n":"Then he shows them a hen and her chicks. The hen has four different calls: one for every day, one for food, one to gather them under her wings, and one to warn of danger."},{"sc":"farm","w":"interpreter","e":"smile","t":"God calls His people in different ways too. Learn to know His voice."},{"sc":"farm","n":"They also see a sheep that stays quiet and patient even when it's treated badly, and a robin that looks pretty but eats nasty spiders. \"Some people look good on the outside, but have bad habits inside,\" says the Interpreter."},{"sc":"house","n":"Then the women are washed, sealed with a mark, and dressed in fine white linen. They look so beautiful that each one thinks the other looks better!"},{"sc":"house","w":"interpreter","e":"smile","t":"You will need protection on the road. So I'm sending my servant with you."},{"sc":"house","n":"In walks a big, strong man in armour, with a sword, a helmet and a shield. His name is {Great-heart}."},{"sc":"road","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"I'll guide you, and I'll protect you. Stay close, and let's go!"}],"quote":{"text":"O deliver me from this muck-rake.","who":"Christiana"},"lesson":{"title":"Look up, and lead the weak","text":"The man with the muck-rake was so busy looking down that he missed a crown. Don't spend your life raking up things that don't last. And notice what the Interpreter did for this family: he gave them Great-heart, a strong leader to guide people who were weaker. Real leaders serve and protect others."},"think":"What 'muck-rake' keeps you looking down: your phone, worries, money? What 'crown' might you be missing?","quiz":[{"q":"What was the man with the muck-rake doing?","o":["Raking up straw and dust, never looking up","Reading a book","Building a house","Sleeping"],"why":"He was so busy with dirt that he missed the crown."},{"q":"What was being offered to him?","o":["A shining crown","A new rake","A bag of gold","A horse"],"why":"A crown, in exchange for his muck-rake. He never looked up to see it."},{"q":"What did the spider in the best room teach?","o":["Faith can bring anyone into the King's house","Spiders are dangerous","Clean your room","Stay away from palaces"],"why":"Proverbs 30:28. Even a spider can be in a king's palace."},{"q":"How many different calls did the hen have?","o":["Four","One","Two","Ten"],"why":"God calls His people in different ways, too."},{"q":"Who did the Interpreter send to guide the family?","o":["Great-heart","Mr Worldly Wiseman","Talkative","Pliable"],"why":"A brave, strong servant to lead and protect them."}]}}},"p2c2":{"challenge":[{"q":"Where did Great-heart explain how pilgrims are forgiven?","o":["At the Cross","At Palace Beautiful","At the gate","In the arbour"],"why":"Where Christian's burden fell off."},{"q":"How are pilgrims pardoned, according to Great-heart?","o":["By what another has done for them","By their own hard work","By paying money","By being born good"],"why":"Someone else paid the price."},{"q":"How did they get clean water from the muddy spring?","o":["Let the mud settle in a cup","Strained it with cloth","Waited for rain","Prayed it clean"],"why":"Patience brings clarity."},{"q":"Who did Great-heart take by the hand on Hill Difficulty?","o":["James, the youngest","Christiana","Mercy","Matthew"],"why":"Leaders go at the pace of the weakest."},{"q":"What did Christiana forget in the arbour?","o":["Her bottle","Her letter","Her coat","Her son"],"why":"Comfort makes us forgetful."},{"q":"Who was standing with the lions?","o":["Giant Grim","Giant Despair","Apollyon","Mr Brisk"],"why":"He tried to block the King's highway."},{"q":"What did the boys do when danger came?","o":["Went behind Great-heart","Ran ahead","Fought the giant","Went home"],"why":"Brave in front, until danger came!"},{"q":"Why did Mr Brisk lose interest in Mercy?","o":["She gave her sewing to the poor","She was too old","She was unkind","She couldn't sew"],"why":"He loved money and looks, not character."},{"q":"What made Matthew sick?","o":["The enemy's fruit he ate earlier","Muddy water","A lion's bite","Too much sleep"],"why":"Sin tastes sweet at first and makes you sick later."},{"q":"Complete: \"Bear ye one another's ___, and so fulfil the law of Christ.\"","o":["burdens","bags","names","crowns"],"why":"Galatians 6:2. Carry each other's loads."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Who came back to guide the family at the end of the chapter?","o":["Great-heart","Evangelist","Giant Grim","Mr Brisk"],"why":"The Interpreter sent him back, just as they asked!"},"choices":[{"title":"Carry the little one","q":"Your class is walking to a sports field 3 km away. One small boy keeps falling behind, and the others are laughing at him.","o":[{"t":"Walk back, walk with him at his pace, and encourage him.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! That's Great-heart taking little James by the hand."},{"t":"Shout at him to hurry up.","f":"Great-heart didn't scold James. He walked with him."},{"t":"Laugh along with the others.","f":"Leaders protect the weak. They don't join the crowd."}]},{"title":"Muddy water","q":"A rumour about a classmate is spreading fast in your WhatsApp groups. You don't know if it's true.","o":[{"t":"Don't share it. Wait, and find out the truth first.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Muddy water needs time to settle before anyone drinks it."},{"t":"Forward it. Everyone else is.","f":"That's drinking muddy water, and serving it to others."},{"t":"Add your own comment to make it funnier.","f":"That stirs up even more mud."}]},{"title":"Character over looks","q":"A popular classmate wants to be your friend, but laughs at you for spending Saturdays tutoring juniors for free. \"You're wasting your time. Come and hang out instead.\"","o":[{"t":"Keep tutoring, and look for friends who value what you value.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Mercy, you won't trade your kindness for popularity."},{"t":"Stop tutoring so they'll like you.","f":"Mercy didn't stop sewing for the poor to please Mr Brisk."},{"t":"Start charging the juniors money.","f":"That's Mr Brisk's idea: \"Sell them!\" Mercy chose to give."}]},{"title":"Take the medicine","q":"For weeks you skipped revision and copied homework. Now the exam is next week and you're completely lost.","o":[{"t":"Tell your teacher the truth, ask for help, and study hard, even if it's tough.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Matthew, take the medicine, even if it's bitter."},{"t":"Hope for the best and say nothing.","f":"Hiding the sickness doesn't cure it."},{"t":"Look for exam expo.","f":"That's the enemy's fruit all over again."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"road","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Part II, Chapter 2 in real life."},{"sc":"cross","n":"✝️ Explain the 'why'. Good leaders teach so even the youngest understand."},{"sc":"climb","n":"🤲 Go at the pace of the weakest. Hold the little one's hand."},{"sc":"lions","n":"🦁 Step forward when danger comes. Stand between the problem and the people you lead."},{"sc":"house","n":"🧵 Choose character over looks: in friends, and one day in a partner."},{"sc":"house","n":"💊 Take the medicine. When a wrong choice catches up with you, get help fast."}],"stops":{"p2c2s1":{"story":[{"sc":"cross","n":"Great-heart leads the family up the road to the place where Christian's burden fell off: the Cross."},{"sc":"cross","w":"christiana","e":"smile","t":"This is where my husband's load rolled away! Great-heart, please explain it to us. How can we be forgiven?"},{"sc":"cross","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"You are forgiven by someone else's goodness. Someone else paid what you owed. The Prince took the punishment, so you could go free."},{"sc":"cross","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"It's like a debt you could never pay. Then a friend pays all of it for you. The {pardon} is real, because the price was really paid."},{"sc":"cross","w":"christiana","e":"big","t":"Now I understand! It makes my heart light. If my husband were here, I'd say: you were right!"},{"sc":"cross","w":"mercy","e":"worried","t":"It makes me want to cry. He loved us THAT much?"},{"sc":"cross","w":"matthew","e":"big","t":"Then let's follow Him all the way!"},{"sc":"cross","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"That's exactly what this journey is for. Love like that makes people brave."}],"quote":{"text":"He hath given me rest by His sorrow, and life by His death.","who":"Christian"},"lesson":{"title":"Teach clearly, lead from gratitude","text":"Great-heart didn't just walk ahead. He stopped and explained things so that even the youngest could understand. And notice what the Cross did: it made everyone grateful and ready to follow. Leaders explain the 'why', and they lead from a thankful heart, not a proud one."},"think":"Who explained something important to you in a way you finally understood? How could you do that for someone younger?","quiz":[{"q":"Where did Great-heart stop to explain forgiveness?","o":["At the Cross","At the gate","At Vanity Fair","At the swamp"],"why":"The place where Christian's burden fell off."},{"q":"According to Great-heart, how are pilgrims forgiven?","o":["Someone else paid what they owed","By working very hard","By being polite","By giving money"],"why":"The Prince took the punishment so they could go free."},{"q":"What picture did Great-heart use?","o":["A friend paying a debt you could never pay","A lion and a lamb","A broken bridge","A storm"],"why":"The pardon is real because the price was really paid."},{"q":"How did Mercy feel?","o":["Moved to tears by such love","Bored","Angry","Scared"],"why":"Real love moves the heart."},{"q":"What does a good leader do, like Great-heart here?","o":["Explains things clearly, even for the youngest","Walks ahead without talking","Keeps secrets","Only talks to adults"],"why":"Leaders make sure everyone understands the 'why'."}]},"p2c2s2":{"story":[{"sc":"climb","n":"At the foot of Hill Difficulty, they find the spring where Christian drank. But enemies have stamped in it, and the water is muddy."},{"sc":"climb","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"Don't drink it like that. Put some in a cup and wait. The mud will sink to the bottom, and the water on top will be clean."},{"sc":"climb","n":"They wait patiently, and the water clears. Then they drink and feel fresh."},{"sc":"climb","n":"The two easy roads, Danger and Destruction, are now blocked with posts, chains and a ditch. But Great-heart says some people still climb over to use them."},{"sc":"climb","w":"greatheart","e":"stern","t":"When people love the easy way, they'll even break through a fence to get to it."},{"sc":"climb","n":"They start up the steep hill. It's hard. Christiana is panting."},{"sc":"climb","w":"christiana","e":"worried","t":"I'm sure this is a breathing hill! No wonder people choose the easy roads."},{"sc":"climb","w":"james","e":"worried","t":"I'm tired! I can't go any more!"},{"sc":"climb","n":"Little James starts to cry. Great-heart doesn't scold him. He walks back, takes James by the hand, and helps him climb, step by step."},{"sc":"climb","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"Come, my boy. We'll go together. The arbour isn't far now."},{"sc":"arbour","n":"Halfway up, they rest in the arbour, the same place where Christian lost his roll. They eat and drink and thank God."},{"sc":"arbour","n":"But when they leave, Christiana forgets her bottle of drink in the arbour! She sends one of the boys back to fetch it."},{"sc":"arbour","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"This is a forgetful place. Christian lost his roll here too. When people get comfortable, they forget things. Rest, but stay alert!"}],"quote":{"text":"I dare say this is a breathing hill.","who":"Christiana"},"lesson":{"title":"Carry the weakest, and wait for clear water","text":"Great-heart didn't leave little James behind or shout at him. He took his hand and climbed at his pace. Leaders of others go at the speed of the slowest, not the fastest. And the muddy spring teaches patience: wait for things to settle before you drink, or decide."},"think":"Who is the 'little James' in your group: a younger sibling, a slower classmate? How could you take their hand this week?","quiz":[{"q":"What had happened to the spring at the foot of the hill?","o":["Enemies had made it muddy","It had dried up","It was poisoned","It had turned to wine"],"why":"But patience made it clear again."},{"q":"How did they get clean water?","o":["They let the mud settle in a cup","They boiled it","They found another spring","They bought water"],"why":"Wait for things to settle, and they become clear."},{"q":"What did Great-heart do when James cried?","o":["Took his hand and climbed with him","Told him to stop crying","Left him behind","Carried Christiana instead"],"why":"Leaders go at the pace of the weakest."},{"q":"What did Christiana forget in the arbour?","o":["Her bottle of drink","Her roll","Her shoes","Her son"],"why":"Comfortable places make people forgetful."},{"q":"What did Christiana call Hill Difficulty?","o":["A breathing hill","An easy hill","A happy hill","A green hill"],"why":"It left everyone out of breath!"}]},"p2c2s3":{"story":[{"sc":"lions","n":"Near the top, they reach the lions that once scared Christian. The boys, who were running ahead, suddenly hide behind Great-heart."},{"sc":"lions","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"Ha! When there's no danger, you love to run in front. When the lions come, you love to be behind!"},{"sc":"lions","n":"But this time there's something worse. A giant called {Giant Grim} is standing with the lions, backing them up, ready to stop the pilgrims."},{"sc":"lions","w":"grim","e":"frown","t":"What are you doing here? This road is closed. Turn back, or the lions will have you!"},{"sc":"lions","w":"greatheart","e":"stern","t":"These women and children are pilgrims. This is the King's highway, and they WILL pass."},{"sc":"lions","w":"grim","e":"frown","t":"Not while I'm standing here!"},{"sc":"lions","n":"Great-heart draws his sword and steps forward. The giant swings a huge club. The women tremble. The boys cry."},{"sc":"lions","n":"Great-heart fights hard. He knocks the giant to his knees, breaks his weapon arm, and defeats him. Giant Grim will never block pilgrims again!"},{"sc":"lions","w":"greatheart","e":"big","t":"Come, follow me! The lions are chained. Keep to the middle of the path."},{"sc":"lions","n":"Everyone walks past the roaring lions, trembling but safe, and arrives at the door of Palace Beautiful."},{"sc":"lions","w":"watchful","e":"big","t":"Great-heart! Welcome back! And who are these?"},{"sc":"lions","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"This is Christiana, Christian's wife, with her four sons, and her friend Mercy. They're pilgrims now."},{"sc":"lions","n":"Now Great-heart must return to the Interpreter, his master. The family begs him to stay, but he goes. \"Ask my Lord, and maybe He will send me back to you.\""}],"quote":{"text":"The boys that went before were glad to cringe behind, for they were afraid of the lions.","who":"The storyteller"},"lesson":{"title":"Stand between danger and the weak","text":"The boys loved being in front until danger came. Then they hid behind Great-heart. That's what true leaders are for: when the giant shows up, they step forward and stand between the danger and the people they lead."},"think":"When something hard happens in your group or family, do you step forward, or step behind?","quiz":[{"q":"What did the boys do when they saw the lions?","o":["Hid behind Great-heart","Ran ahead","Fought the lions","Went home"],"why":"Brave in front when it's safe; behind when it's scary!"},{"q":"Who was backing up the lions?","o":["Giant Grim","Apollyon","Giant Despair","Mr Brisk"],"why":"Giant Grim tried to block the road."},{"q":"What did Great-heart say about the road?","o":["It was the King's highway, and the pilgrims would pass","It was closed","It was too dangerous","They should find another way"],"why":"He stood his ground for the people he led."},{"q":"What happened to Giant Grim?","o":["Great-heart defeated him","He ran away","He became a pilgrim","He fell asleep"],"why":"The protector did his job."},{"q":"Why did Great-heart leave the family at Palace Beautiful?","o":["He had to return to his master, the Interpreter","He was tired of them","He was scared","He got lost"],"why":"But he told them to ask, and maybe he'd be sent back."}]},"p2c2s4":{"story":[{"sc":"house","n":"The family stays at Palace Beautiful for a whole month. They learn a lot, and they rest."},{"sc":"house","w":"prudence","e":"smile","t":"Boys, let's see what you know. Matthew, who made you? And James, what does God do for us?"},{"sc":"house","n":"The boys answer well. Prudence smiles at Christiana: \"You've taught them well. Keep teaching them, and let them listen to good people.\""},{"sc":"house","n":"Mercy is never idle. She spends her time sewing coats and clothes for poor people."},{"sc":"house","n":"A young man named {Mr Brisk} comes visiting. He's busy, stylish, and he wants to marry Mercy. He sees her sewing all day."},{"sc":"house","w":"brisk","e":"smile","t":"What are you making? Will you sell them? You could make good money!"},{"sc":"house","w":"mercy","e":"smile","t":"No, I give them away to poor people. I'd rather be rich in good deeds."},{"sc":"house","w":"brisk","e":"frown","t":"Give them AWAY? She's a pretty girl, but she has strange habits. I'm off!"},{"sc":"house","w":"mercy","e":"smile","t":"I'm glad he left. I'd rather stay single than marry someone who doesn't love what I love. He loved my looks, not my heart."},{"sc":"house","n":"Then trouble: Matthew falls very sick with terrible stomach pains. It's the fruit from the enemy's garden! He ate it weeks ago, and now it's hurting him."},{"sc":"house","n":"They call a wise old doctor, {Mr Skill}. He tries one medicine, but it isn't strong enough."},{"sc":"house","w":"skill","e":"smile","t":"Matthew needs a special medicine, made from the body and blood of Christ, taken with a promise and a little salt. It's the only thing that will cure him."},{"sc":"house","n":"Matthew doesn't want to take it. It's bitter! But his mother tastes it first to encourage him, and he swallows it. Soon the pain goes, and he's well again!"},{"sc":"house","w":"christiana","e":"smile","t":"Sin always tastes sweet at first, and makes you sick later. I'm so thankful there's a cure."},{"sc":"view","n":"Before they leave, they're shown amazing things: {Jacob's ladder} with angels going up and down, and a {golden anchor} they can take with them, for hope."},{"sc":"road","n":"And then the best news. Great-heart walks up the road! The Interpreter has sent him back to guide them the rest of the way. Everyone cheers!"}],"quote":{"text":"I might have had husbands afore now, though I spake not of it to any; but they were such as did not like my conditions.","who":"Mercy"},"lesson":{"title":"Character over looks, and cures over hiding","text":"Mercy used her hands to serve the poor, and she refused someone who only liked her looks. Choose friends, and later a partner, who love what you love. And Matthew's sickness shows that wrong choices come back later. Leaders don't hide their 'sickness': they get help and take the medicine."},"think":"What do you want people to like about you: your looks and things, or your heart and character?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Mercy do with her time at Palace Beautiful?","o":["Sewed clothes for poor people","Slept","Played games","Went shopping"],"why":"Her hands were busy with kindness."},{"q":"Why did Mr Brisk stop visiting Mercy?","o":["She gave her work away instead of selling it","She was rude","She moved away","He got sick"],"why":"He liked her looks, not her heart."},{"q":"Why did Matthew get sick?","o":["He ate fruit from the enemy's garden weeks before","He caught a cold","He fell down","He ate too much bread"],"why":"Wrong choices can make us sick later."},{"q":"Who was the doctor?","o":["Mr Skill","Mr Legality","Great-heart","Mr Honest"],"why":"A wise doctor who knew the right medicine."},{"q":"What did they receive to take with them for hope?","o":["A golden anchor","A silver coin","A sword","A map"],"why":"Hope is an anchor for the soul (Hebrews 6:19)."}]}}},"p2c3":{"challenge":[{"q":"What did the shepherd boy sing?","o":["\"He that is down needs fear no fall\"","\"What shall I do?\"","\"We buy the truth\"","\"Set down my name\""],"why":"A song about humility."},{"q":"What did Great-heart say the shepherd boy had more of than a rich man?","o":["Peace in his heart","Money","Sheep","Friends"],"why":"The flower called heart's-ease."},{"q":"Why was the Valley of Humiliation beautiful to Mercy?","o":["It was quiet and peaceful","It had shops","It had a palace","It had a river"],"why":"Humble places are peaceful places."},{"q":"What happened when Great-heart faced the lion in the dark valley?","o":["It went away","It attacked","It fell asleep","It followed them"],"why":"Resist the devil, and he will flee."},{"q":"What did the family do in the thick darkness?","o":["Prayed together","Separated","Went back","Lit a fire"],"why":"They called out to God together."},{"q":"What did Giant Maul call Great-heart?","o":["A kidnapper","A coward","A thief","A liar"],"why":"Critics sometimes twist good things into bad."},{"q":"Great-heart said his business was to...","o":["Persuade people to turn back to God","Fight giants for fun","Make money","Become famous"],"why":"He knew his 'why'."},{"q":"Where was Mr Honest from?","o":["Stupidity","Vanity","Beulah","Carnal Policy"],"why":"A cold town, but God warmed his heart."},{"q":"How long did Mr Fearing lie at the Slough of Despond?","o":["More than a month","One hour","One day","One year"],"why":"He was afraid, but he didn't go back."},{"q":"Complete: \"Comfort the feebleminded, support the weak, be ___ toward all men.\"","o":["patient","strong","rich","quick"],"why":"1 Thessalonians 5:14."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Mr Fearing carried a 'Slough of ___' in his mind.","o":["Despond","Water","Mud","Fear"],"why":"A swamp of discouragement he took everywhere, but he still made it home."},"choices":[{"title":"Down and humble","q":"Results are out. You came first in your class. Your desk-mate came last and looks close to tears.","o":[{"t":"Celebrate quietly, then encourage your desk-mate and offer to study together.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! \"He that is humble ever shall have God to be his guide.\""},{"t":"Post your result everywhere.","f":"That's the slip on the way down into the valley. Stay humble."},{"t":"Ignore your desk-mate.","f":"A humble leader notices the one who is hurting."}]},{"title":"When critics twist things","q":"You start a lunchtime Bible club. Some classmates say you're only doing it to show off and act \"holier than thou\".","o":[{"t":"Kindly explain why you started it, invite them, and keep going.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Great-heart with Giant Maul: know your 'why', say it calmly, keep going."},{"t":"Stop the club so they'll stop talking.","f":"Great-heart didn't stop guiding pilgrims because of Maul's accusations."},{"t":"Argue loudly and insult them.","f":"Answer \"with meekness\", says 1 Peter 3:15."}]},{"title":"The fearful friend","q":"Your friend has to give a class presentation tomorrow. She's terrified and says she'll fake being sick.","o":[{"t":"Practise with her tonight, and promise to sit where she can see you.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Great-heart with Mr Fearing: patience, not pressure."},{"t":"Tell her to stop being a baby.","f":"Fearful people need gentleness, not mocking."},{"t":"Help her fake being sick.","f":"That keeps her stuck in the Slough. Help her through it instead."}]},{"title":"The dark valley","q":"Your little sister watched a scary film and now can't sleep. She keeps crying at night.","o":[{"t":"Sit with her, comfort her, pray together, and keep scary films away.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! In the dark valley, nobody should be left alone."},{"t":"Tell her to stop crying and sleep.","f":"Great-heart stayed close when the boys were scared."},{"t":"Laugh at her for being scared.","f":"Fearful people need patience, not jokes."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"valley","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Part II, Chapter 3 in real life."},{"sc":"valley","n":"🌼 Stay humble. Humble people have peace that money can't buy."},{"sc":"shadow","n":"🔦 Don't leave anyone alone in the dark. Walk with people through hard times."},{"sc":"cave","n":"💬 Know your 'why'. When people twist your good intentions, answer calmly, and keep going."},{"sc":"oak","n":"🌳 Be patient with the fearful. Some people need more time. Walk at their pace."}],"stops":{"p2c3s1":{"story":[{"sc":"valley","n":"Great-heart leads the family down the hill into the Valley of Humiliation, the valley where Christian fought Apollyon."},{"sc":"valley","w":"christiana","e":"worried","t":"Is this the valley where my husband almost died? I'm scared."},{"sc":"valley","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"Don't be afraid. Christian met Apollyon here because he slipped on the way down. For {humble} people, this is one of the most beautiful valleys in the whole land."},{"sc":"valley","n":"And it IS beautiful: green meadows, lilies, and quiet fields. Mercy loves it."},{"sc":"valley","w":"mercy","e":"big","t":"I love this place! It's peaceful. No noise, no crowds. Just quiet."},{"sc":"valley","n":"Then they hear singing. A boy in old, worn-out clothes is looking after his father's sheep, and singing to himself."},{"sc":"valley","w":"shepherdboy","e":"big","t":"He that is down needs fear no fall, he that is low no pride; he that is humble ever shall have God to be his guide.","b":true},{"sc":"valley","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"Listen to him! That boy has very little. But I promise you, he has more peace in his heart than a rich man dressed in silk and velvet."},{"sc":"valley","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"He wears the flower called {heart's-ease}. You can't buy it. You only find it when you're humble."},{"sc":"valley","n":"They pass the place where Christian fought Apollyon. A stone marks the spot, so pilgrims will remember his victory. Matthew and James stare at it in wonder."}],"quote":{"text":"He that is down needs fear no fall, He that is low no pride; He that is humble ever shall Have God to be his guide.","who":"The shepherd boy"},"lesson":{"title":"Humble people lead with peace","text":"Christian fought Apollyon here because he slipped on the way down. But the shepherd boy, with almost nothing, sang with joy. Humble leaders don't need to prove themselves or be noticed. They're not afraid of falling, because they're already low. And they carry peace that money can't buy."},"think":"When did you feel truly at peace? Was it about what you had, or something deeper?","quiz":[{"q":"Why did Christian meet Apollyon in this valley, according to Great-heart?","o":["He slipped on the way down","He went looking for him","He was lost","Apollyon lived there"],"why":"Pride can make you slip. Humility keeps your footing."},{"q":"What was the shepherd boy wearing?","o":["Old, worn-out clothes","Silk and velvet","Shining armour","A crown"],"why":"Poor in things, but rich in peace."},{"q":"Complete the song: \"He that is down needs fear no ___.\"","o":["fall","lion","night","giant"],"why":"If you're already low, there's nowhere to fall."},{"q":"What flower did Great-heart say the boy wore?","o":["Heart's-ease","A rose","A lily","A sunflower"],"why":"Peace in the heart, found only by the humble."},{"q":"What did Mercy love about the valley?","o":["It was peaceful and quiet","It was full of people","It had a market","It had a castle"],"why":"Humble places are often the most peaceful."}]},"p2c3s2":{"story":[{"sc":"shadow","n":"Next comes the Valley of the Shadow of Death. As they enter, they hear groaning, like people in great pain. The ground shakes under their feet."},{"sc":"shadow","w":"james","e":"shock","t":"Mum, I'm scared! What's that noise?"},{"sc":"shadow","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"Stay close to me, boys. Keep walking."},{"sc":"shadow","n":"Then something hisses at them from the dark: a fiend. And a lion comes roaring towards them!"},{"sc":"shadow","n":"Great-heart steps in front of everyone and faces the lion. It stops... turns... and goes away."},{"sc":"shadow","w":"greatheart","e":"stern","t":"Resist the devil, and he will flee from you."},{"sc":"shadow","n":"Then a thick mist comes down. It's so dark they can't see each other. In front of them is a pit, and they can't see the bottom."},{"sc":"shadow","w":"greatheart","e":"worried","t":"This is like doing business in great waters, or going down into the deep. But the light is coming. Let's pray."},{"sc":"shadow","n":"So they all cry out to God, together. And slowly, light comes, and the way ahead appears."},{"sc":"shadow","w":"christiana","e":"worried","t":"Now I understand what my poor husband went through here, all alone. We have Great-heart, and we have each other."},{"sc":"dawn","n":"They come out of the valley in the light. Everyone is tired, but safe. Nobody was left behind."}],"quote":{"text":"This is like doing business in great waters, or like going down into the deep.","who":"Greatheart"},"lesson":{"title":"Stay together in the dark","text":"Christian walked this valley alone. Christiana's family walked it together, with a guide in front. When the lion came, Great-heart stepped forward. When the dark came, they all prayed together. Good leaders don't just survive dark times. They make sure nobody is left behind in them."},"think":"Who could you walk alongside, so they don't go through a hard time alone?","quiz":[{"q":"What did the family hear as they entered the valley?","o":["Groaning, and the ground shaking","Birds singing","Music and dancing","Nothing at all"],"why":"It was a frightening place."},{"q":"What did Great-heart do when the lion came?","o":["Stepped in front and faced it, and it went away","Ran away","Told everyone to hide","Gave it food"],"why":"Resist the devil, and he will flee."},{"q":"What did they do when the thick darkness came?","o":["They prayed together","They went back","They split up","They slept"],"why":"Together, they called out to God, and light came."},{"q":"What did Christiana realise?","o":["How hard it was for Christian to walk this valley alone","That the valley was easy","That she wanted to go home","That Great-heart was afraid"],"why":"Walking together makes the dark easier."},{"q":"How many people were left behind in the valley?","o":["Nobody","One","Two","All the boys"],"why":"A good leader brings everyone through."}]},"p2c3s3":{"story":[{"sc":"cave","n":"At the end of the valley is a cave. Out of it comes {Giant Maul}, a giant who attacks young pilgrims, not just with his club, but with twisted, clever words."},{"sc":"cave","w":"maul","e":"frown","t":"Great-heart! How many times have I told you to stop doing this?"},{"sc":"cave","w":"greatheart","e":"stern","t":"Doing what?"},{"sc":"cave","w":"maul","e":"frown","t":"You're a kidnapper! You gather up women and children and drag them off to a strange country. You're ruining my master's kingdom!"},{"sc":"cave","w":"greatheart","e":"stern","t":"I am a servant of the God of heaven. My business is to persuade people to turn back to God. I lead them, I don't force them. And I'll keep doing it.","b":true},{"sc":"cave","n":"Giant Maul roars and swings his heavy club. The first blow knocks Great-heart down to one knee! The women scream."},{"sc":"cave","n":"Christiana and Mercy, and the boys, start praying out loud."},{"sc":"cave","n":"Great-heart gets back up. They fight for a long time, resting and fighting again. At last, Great-heart strikes the giant down. Giant Maul will never trouble pilgrims again."},{"sc":"cave","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"Thank you for praying. I felt it. We won that battle together."},{"sc":"road","n":"They put up a sign there, so other pilgrims will know the road is safe now."}],"quote":{"text":"I am a servant of the God of heaven; my business is to persuade sinners to repentance.","who":"Greatheart"},"lesson":{"title":"Know your 'why' when critics come","text":"Giant Maul twisted the truth: he called Great-heart a kidnapper for helping people. Leaders who do good will sometimes be accused of bad motives. Great-heart answered calmly and clearly: who he served, and why he did it. Then he kept going. And he won partly because the people he led were praying for him."},"think":"If someone said you were doing a good thing for a bad reason, what would you say back?","quiz":[{"q":"How did Giant Maul attack young pilgrims?","o":["With a club AND with twisted, clever words","With fire","With a bow and arrow","With money"],"why":"Lies can hurt as much as weapons."},{"q":"What did Giant Maul accuse Great-heart of?","o":["Being a kidnapper","Being lazy","Stealing money","Telling jokes"],"why":"He twisted good leadership into something bad."},{"q":"How did Great-heart answer?","o":["He explained who he served and why he led people","He shouted insults","He ran away","He said nothing"],"why":"Know your 'why' and say it clearly."},{"q":"What did the women and boys do during the fight?","o":["They prayed out loud","They ran away","They helped the giant","They slept"],"why":"Followers can strengthen their leader through prayer."},{"q":"Who won the fight?","o":["Great-heart","Giant Maul","Nobody","The boys"],"why":"He was knocked down, but he got back up."}]},"p2c3s4":{"story":[{"sc":"oak","n":"A little further on, they find an old pilgrim fast asleep under an oak tree."},{"sc":"oak","n":"Great-heart wakes him gently. The old man jumps up, thinking they're robbers!"},{"sc":"oak","w":"honest","e":"shock","t":"Who are you? What do you want? I have nothing worth stealing!"},{"sc":"oak","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"Calm down, father. We're pilgrims too. What's your name?"},{"sc":"oak","w":"honest","e":"smile","t":"Not Honesty in the abstract, but Honest is my name; and I wish that my nature shall agree to what I am called.","b":true},{"sc":"oak","w":"honest","e":"smile","t":"I come from the town of {Stupidity}. It's a cold, dull place. But even a heart from Stupidity can be warmed by God!"},{"sc":"oak","w":"honest","e":"smile","t":"Great-heart, tell me: did you ever know a man called {Mr Fearing}?"},{"sc":"oak","w":"greatheart","e":"big","t":"Know him? I was his guide all the way to the Celestial City! He was the most fearful pilgrim I ever met."},{"sc":"swamp","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"He lay at the Slough of Despond for more than a month. He was too scared to cross, even when others offered to help."},{"sc":"gate","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"At the Wicket Gate, he was too scared to knock. He stood outside, shaking, until the Keeper came out and brought him in himself."},{"sc":"oak","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"He had, I think, a Slough of Despond in his mind; a swamp he carried with him everywhere."},{"sc":"valley","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"But here's the strange thing. In the Valley of Humiliation, he was perfectly happy. And at Vanity Fair, he was so bold, I had to hold him back!"},{"sc":"deepriver","w":"greatheart","e":"big","t":"And at the end, at the river he was SO afraid of, the water was lower than I've ever seen it. He crossed with hardly wet feet!"},{"sc":"oak","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"God was very gentle with him. And I learned to be gentle with him too. Fearful people need patience, not pressure."}],"quote":{"text":"He had, I think, a Slough of Despond in his mind; a slough that he carried everywhere with him.","who":"Greatheart"},"lesson":{"title":"Lead fearful people with patience","text":"Mr Fearing was afraid of almost everything, but he never turned back. Great-heart didn't mock him or push him. He walked with him patiently, and God made the river low for him at the end. Leaders don't only lead the bold. They make room for the fearful, and they're gentle with them."},"think":"Do you know someone who is very fearful or anxious? How could you be patient with them, like Great-heart?","quiz":[{"q":"Where did they find Mr Honest?","o":["Asleep under an oak tree","At Vanity Fair","In a cave","In the swamp"],"why":"An old pilgrim taking a rest."},{"q":"Which town was Mr Honest from?","o":["Stupidity","Vanity","Morality","Destruction"],"why":"Even people from the coldest places can become pilgrims."},{"q":"What was Mr Fearing's biggest problem?","o":["He was afraid of almost everything","He was lazy","He was proud","He was greedy"],"why":"He carried a 'Slough of Despond' in his mind."},{"q":"How did Mr Fearing get through the Wicket Gate?","o":["The Keeper came out and brought him in","He climbed over","He knocked loudly","Great-heart pushed him"],"why":"God meets fearful people where they are."},{"q":"What was the river like when Mr Fearing crossed?","o":["The lowest it had ever been","Deeper than ever","Frozen","Full of crocodiles"],"why":"God was very gentle with him."}]}}},"p2c4":{"challenge":[{"q":"What was Gaius's inn known for?","o":["Welcoming pilgrims for free","Expensive food","Its silver mine","Its giant"],"why":"A generous home on the road."},{"q":"\"The more he cast away, the more he had\" describes...","o":["A generous person who gives to the poor","A thief","A lazy man","A fisherman"],"why":"Gaius solved Honest's riddle."},{"q":"Who married Mercy?","o":["Matthew","James","Great-heart","Mr Honest"],"why":"Mercy joined the family for good!"},{"q":"What did Mr Feeble-mind resolve to do?","o":["Run, walk, or creep, but never stop","Go home","Fight every giant","Sleep until he was stronger"],"why":"One of the bravest promises in the book."},{"q":"How did Mr Ready-to-halt walk?","o":["On crutches","On a horse","Very fast","With a sword"],"why":"Slow, but faithful."},{"q":"How had Vanity changed?","o":["It had good people in it, and was kinder to pilgrims","It was the same","It was empty","It was a castle"],"why":"Faithful's light changed the town."},{"q":"What did the monster at Vanity do?","o":["Snatched children","Stole silver","Burned houses","Ate fruit"],"why":"The pilgrims fought for the town's children."},{"q":"What did Great-heart's team do to Doubting Castle?","o":["Tore it down completely","Moved into it","Painted it","Locked it"],"why":"So it could never trap pilgrims again."},{"q":"Who did they free from the dungeon?","o":["Mr Despondency and Much-afraid","Christian and Hopeful","Giant Despair","Demas"],"why":"Prisoners of despair, set free."},{"q":"Complete: \"Thou hast turned for me my mourning into ___.\"","o":["dancing","singing","laughing","running"],"why":"Psalm 30:11."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Mr Ready-to-halt danced with one ___ in his hand.","o":["crutch","sword","cup","flower"],"why":"\"But I promise you he footed it well.\""},"choices":[{"title":"The riddle in real life","q":"You have ₦2,000 pocket money saved. A classmate can't buy the textbook everyone needs for the exam.","o":[{"t":"Help him get the book: give some money, share yours, or ask an adult to help.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! \"He that bestows his goods upon the poor, shall have as much again, and ten times more.\""},{"t":"Keep your money. It's not your problem.","f":"Gaius's inn was open to everyone who needed it."},{"t":"Lend it to him with interest.","f":"That's Mr Brisk thinking. Generosity doesn't charge extra."}]},{"title":"Make room","q":"You're the captain of the class quiz team. A quiet classmate who learns slowly asks to join. Your teammates groan.","o":[{"t":"Welcome her, find what she's good at, and give her a real role.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Great-heart's team made room for Mr Feeble-mind."},{"t":"Say the team is full.","f":"Nobody gets left behind on this road."},{"t":"Let her join, but never let her answer.","f":"Making room means giving people a real place."}]},{"title":"The monster","q":"Someone in the school WhatsApp group keeps posting cruel messages about the juniors. Some juniors have stopped coming to school.","o":[{"t":"Stand with others: screenshot it, report it to a teacher, and support the juniors.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! The monster was beaten by people standing together, again and again."},{"t":"Leave the group and say nothing.","f":"The pilgrims didn't walk away from the town's children."},{"t":"Post insults back.","f":"Fighting cruelty with cruelty feeds the monster."}]},{"title":"Pulling down the castle","q":"Your friend failed JAMB and now says, \"I'm useless. I'll never get into university.\" He's stopped going out.","o":[{"t":"Visit him with friends, remind him of his strengths, help him plan, and celebrate small steps.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! That's tearing down Doubting Castle together, and then dancing!"},{"t":"Wait for him to feel better on his own.","f":"Great-heart went to the castle. He didn't wait for the prisoners to escape."},{"t":"Agree that it's hopeless.","f":"That's Giant Despair talking. There is a key called Promise."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"inn","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Part II, Chapter 4 in real life."},{"sc":"inn","n":"🍽️ Be generous. People who give don't run out. They get richer in the things that matter."},{"sc":"inn","n":"🐢 Run, walk, or creep, but never stop. And make room for those who creep."},{"sc":"beast","n":"🐉 Stand together. Monsters like bullying are beaten by people who stand together, again and again."},{"sc":"ruins","n":"🏚️ Go back for the prisoners. Help others out of the despair you escaped, and celebrate every rescue!"}],"stops":{"p2c4s1":{"story":[{"sc":"road","n":"The pilgrims are tired. Mr Honest knows a good place to stay: the inn of {Gaius}, a man famous for welcoming pilgrims."},{"sc":"inn","w":"gaius","e":"big","t":"Come in, come in! Christian's family? Welcome! You will stay as long as you need, and it won't cost you a thing."},{"sc":"inn","n":"Gaius cooks them a huge meal. Around the table, they talk, laugh, and tell stories about all the brave pilgrims who went before them."},{"sc":"inn","w":"honest","e":"smile","t":"Gaius, I have a riddle for you!"},{"sc":"inn","w":"honest","e":"big","t":"A man there was, though some did count him mad, the more he cast away, the more he had.","b":true},{"sc":"inn","n":"Everyone thinks hard. What kind of man gets richer by throwing things away?"},{"sc":"inn","w":"gaius","e":"big","t":"He that bestows his goods upon the poor, shall have as much again, and ten times more!","b":true},{"sc":"inn","w":"honest","e":"big","t":"That's it! The generous person never runs out."},{"sc":"inn","n":"The family stays at the inn for a long time. While they're there, Matthew marries Mercy, and James marries Gaius's daughter Phoebe. Christiana's family is growing!"},{"sc":"inn","w":"christiana","e":"smile","t":"I never imagined, when I left home, that God would give us so much on the way."}],"quote":{"text":"A man there was, though some did count him mad, The more he cast away, the more he had.","who":"Honest"},"lesson":{"title":"Generous leaders never run out","text":"Gaius opened his home and his table to pilgrims for free. The riddle explains why he wasn't worried: people who give to others end up richer, not poorer. Leaders who are generous with their time, help and things build homes where others can rest and grow."},"think":"What could you give this week: your time, help with homework, something you own? Who needs it?","quiz":[{"q":"What was Gaius famous for?","o":["Welcoming pilgrims into his inn for free","Fighting giants","Selling silver","Building castles"],"why":"His home was open to anyone on the journey."},{"q":"Who asked the riddle?","o":["Mr Honest","Great-heart","Christiana","James"],"why":"Old Honest loved a good riddle."},{"q":"What was the answer to the riddle?","o":["The person who gives to the poor ends up with more","A thief","A farmer","A king"],"why":"Give generously, and you'll have \"ten times more\"."},{"q":"Who did Matthew marry?","o":["Mercy","Phoebe","Much-afraid","Prudence"],"why":"Mercy, who came along without an invitation, became part of the family!"},{"q":"What does \"the liberal soul shall be made fat\" mean?","o":["Generous people will be blessed","Eat a lot","Spend all your money","Don't share"],"why":"Proverbs 11:25. 'Liberal' here means generous."}]},"p2c4s2":{"story":[{"sc":"inn","n":"One day, news comes to the inn: a giant called {Giant Slay-good} is attacking pilgrims on the road nearby."},{"sc":"inn","w":"greatheart","e":"stern","t":"Then let's go and stop him. Who's coming with me?"},{"sc":"inn","n":"Mr Honest, Gaius, and Christiana's four sons all grab weapons and follow Great-heart."},{"sc":"cave","n":"They find the giant at his cave. He has caught a weak, thin pilgrim and is about to hurt him."},{"sc":"cave","w":"slaygood","e":"frown","t":"What do you want? This one is mine!"},{"sc":"cave","w":"greatheart","e":"stern","t":"We've come to rescue the pilgrims you've captured. Let him go!"},{"sc":"cave","n":"They fight for an hour. At last, Great-heart defeats the giant, and they free the captured pilgrim."},{"sc":"cave","w":"feeble","e":"worried","t":"Thank you! My name is {Mr Feeble-mind}. I'm weak, and slow, and afraid of many things. I'm not much of a pilgrim."},{"sc":"cave","w":"feeble","e":"smile","t":"But I have resolved to run when I can, to go when I cannot run, and to creep when I cannot go.","b":true},{"sc":"inn","n":"They bring him back to the inn. While they're eating, another pilgrim arrives, walking on two crutches. His name is {Mr Ready-to-halt}."},{"sc":"inn","w":"halt","e":"smile","t":"I'm slow too, brother. Let's go together. I'll lend you one of my crutches if you need it!"},{"sc":"inn","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"You're both welcome to travel with us. We'll go at your pace. Nobody gets left behind on this road."}],"quote":{"text":"I have resolved to run when I can, to go when I cannot run, and to creep when I cannot go.","who":"Feeble"},"lesson":{"title":"Make room for the weak","text":"Mr Feeble-mind thought he wasn't much of a pilgrim. But his promise is one of the bravest in the book: run, walk, or creep, but never stop. Great-heart's team didn't just rescue him; they welcomed him and Mr Ready-to-halt, and slowed down for them. Great teams make room for people who are slower or weaker."},"think":"Is there someone in your class or church who feels 'not good enough'? How could you make room for them?","quiz":[{"q":"Who went with Great-heart to fight Giant Slay-good?","o":["Mr Honest, Gaius and Christiana's sons","Only Mercy","Nobody","Mr Brisk"],"why":"A team of brave men, young and old."},{"q":"Who did they rescue from the giant?","o":["Mr Feeble-mind","Mr Honest","Evangelist","Pliable"],"why":"A weak pilgrim who needed help."},{"q":"Complete Mr Feeble-mind's promise: \"Run when I can, go when I cannot run, and ___ when I cannot go.\"","o":["creep","sleep","stop","cry"],"why":"Never stop, even if you have to creep."},{"q":"How did Mr Ready-to-halt walk?","o":["On two crutches","Very fast","On a horse","Backwards"],"why":"Slow, but still on the road."},{"q":"What did Great-heart promise the slow pilgrims?","o":["They'd go at their pace, and nobody would be left behind","They'd have to keep up","They could ride","They should go home"],"why":"Strong people carry the weak."}]},"p2c4s3":{"story":[{"sc":"fair","n":"The pilgrims arrive at the town of Vanity, the place where Faithful died. But something has changed."},{"sc":"fair","n":"They stay with an old pilgrim named {Mnason}. He introduces them to other good people who now live in the town: Mr Contrite, Mr Holy-man, Mr Love-saint, Mr Dare-not-lie and Mr Penitent."},{"sc":"fair","w":"mnason","e":"smile","t":"Faithful's death changed many hearts here. The town is much kinder to pilgrims now than it used to be."},{"sc":"beast","n":"But there's a problem. A terrible monster keeps coming out of the woods. It has a body like a dragon, seven heads and ten horns. It snatches the town's children!"},{"sc":"beast","w":"greatheart","e":"stern","t":"Then we will fight it. Who's with me?"},{"sc":"beast","n":"Great-heart, Mr Honest, Mnason, and the brave men of Vanity go out together to meet the monster."},{"sc":"beast","n":"The monster attacks. They fight it hard and wound it, again and again. It runs back into the woods."},{"sc":"beast","n":"Every time it comes back, they fight it again. And every time, it's weaker. In the end it hardly dares come out, and the children are safe."},{"sc":"fair","n":"The people of Vanity love the pilgrims for it. While they're there, Samuel marries Mnason's daughter Grace, and Joseph marries her sister Martha."},{"sc":"fair","w":"christiana","e":"smile","t":"My husband was mocked and Faithful was killed in this town. Now pilgrims are loved here. God has turned it around!"}],"quote":{"text":"We buy the truth.","who":"Faithful"},"lesson":{"title":"Light changes a town","text":"Faithful stood for the truth here and paid with his life. Years later, Vanity has good people in it, and is kinder to pilgrims. Then the pilgrims didn't just protect themselves. They protected the town's children from the monster. Leaders shine a light that changes places, and they fight for people who can't fight for themselves."},"think":"What 'monster' is hurting children or young people in your area, such as bullying or drugs? How could people stand together against it?","quiz":[{"q":"How was Vanity different this time?","o":["It had good people in it, and was kinder to pilgrims","It was exactly the same","It was empty","It had burned down"],"why":"Faithful's courage changed many hearts."},{"q":"Who did the pilgrims stay with in Vanity?","o":["Mnason","Lord Hate-good","Demas","Mr Brisk"],"why":"A good old pilgrim living in the town."},{"q":"What was the monster doing?","o":["Snatching the town's children","Selling goods","Guarding the gate","Sleeping"],"why":"It preyed on the weakest."},{"q":"How was the monster defeated?","o":["They fought it together again and again, until it was too weak to come out","One big battle","They paid it to leave","It ran away on its own"],"why":"Standing together, again and again."},{"q":"Who did Samuel marry?","o":["Grace, Mnason's daughter","Phoebe","Mercy","Much-afraid"],"why":"The family kept growing on the road!"}]},"p2c4s4":{"story":[{"sc":"silver","n":"They pass the hill Lucre, where Demas still calls to pilgrims, and the pillar of salt. They don't stop."},{"sc":"meadow","n":"Then they reach the fence by By-path Meadow, where Christian and Hopeful once went the wrong way. They read the warning sign Christian put up."},{"sc":"meadow","w":"greatheart","e":"stern","t":"Giant Despair still lives in Doubting Castle, and he still catches pilgrims. I think it's time we pulled that castle down."},{"sc":"meadow","w":"honest","e":"big","t":"I'm with you!"},{"sc":"castle","n":"So Great-heart, Mr Honest and the four young men march to Doubting Castle, while the women, the children and the weaker pilgrims wait safely on the road."},{"sc":"castle","w":"despair","e":"frown","t":"Who dares to knock at my castle?"},{"sc":"castle","w":"greatheart","e":"stern","t":"Great-heart, the King's guide. You've kept pilgrims prisoner long enough. Come out and fight!"},{"sc":"castle","n":"Giant Despair comes out in armour with a huge club. It's a hard fight, but Great-heart and his friends defeat him, and his wife Diffidence too."},{"sc":"dungeon","n":"Inside, they search the dungeons. They find two prisoners, nearly starved: {Mr Despondency} and his daughter {Much-afraid}."},{"sc":"dungeon","w":"despondency","e":"worried","t":"Are you real? Are we really free?"},{"sc":"castle","n":"It takes them seven days, but they tear Doubting Castle down to the ground."},{"sc":"ruins","n":"Back on the road, everyone celebrates! Christiana plays a viol, Mercy plays a lute, and they all sing."},{"sc":"ruins","n":"And Mr Ready-to-halt takes Much-afraid by the hand and dances with her. He can't dance without one crutch in his hand, but he dances well!"},{"sc":"ruins","w":"muchafraid","e":"big","t":"I've never been so happy in my life!"}],"quote":{"text":"He could not dance without one crutch in his hand; but I promise you he footed it well.","who":"The storyteller"},"lesson":{"title":"Don't just escape despair, defeat it","text":"Christian and Hopeful escaped Doubting Castle. Great-heart's team went back and tore it down, so it couldn't trap anyone else, and they set its prisoners free. Then they danced! Leaders don't just survive hard things. They go back to help others who are still trapped, and they celebrate every rescue."},"think":"Who might be stuck in their own 'Doubting Castle'? What could you and your friends do together to help them out?","quiz":[{"q":"Why did Great-heart decide to attack Doubting Castle?","o":["Giant Despair was still trapping pilgrims","He wanted the treasure","He was bored","Christiana asked him to"],"why":"He wanted to stop it trapping anyone else."},{"q":"Who waited safely on the road during the fight?","o":["The women, children and weaker pilgrims","Nobody","Great-heart","Giant Despair"],"why":"A good leader protects the vulnerable."},{"q":"Who did they find in the dungeons?","o":["Mr Despondency and his daughter Much-afraid","Christian and Hopeful","Mr Brisk","Gaius"],"why":"Two prisoners of despair, now set free."},{"q":"How long did it take to tear the castle down?","o":["Seven days","One hour","One year","It's still standing"],"why":"They made sure it could never trap anyone again."},{"q":"Who danced with Much-afraid?","o":["Mr Ready-to-halt, with one crutch in his hand","Great-heart","Matthew","Mr Honest"],"why":"He couldn't dance without his crutch, but he danced well!"}]}}},"p2c5":{"challenge":[{"q":"What happened to dirt thrown at the man on Mount Innocent?","o":["It wouldn't stick","It covered him","It turned gold","He threw it back"],"why":"A good life outlasts lies."},{"q":"What did Mercy's mirror show?","o":["Her face, and the face of the Prince","The future","Only the sky","Her house"],"why":"The Word of God shows us ourselves, and Jesus."},{"q":"How many men did Valiant-for-truth fight?","o":["Three","One","Seven","Ten"],"why":"Three to one, and he held his ground."},{"q":"What was the secret of his Jerusalem blade?","o":["He held it tightly","It was magic","It was new","It was gold"],"why":"Hold on to God's Word."},{"q":"\"Who would true valour see, let him come ___.\"","o":["hither","home","later","back"],"why":"\"Hither\" means \"here\"."},{"q":"Who were asleep on the Enchanted Ground?","o":["Heedless and Too-bold","Faithful and Hopeful","Matthew and Mercy","Gaius and Honest"],"why":"They stopped watching."},{"q":"What did Mr Stand-fast do when Madam Bubble tempted him?","o":["Got on his knees and prayed","Followed her","Ran away screaming","Bought something"],"why":"Watch and pray."},{"q":"What were Christiana's words as she entered the river?","o":["\"I come, Lord, to be with Thee, and bless Thee!\"","\"What shall I do?\"","\"Grace reigns!\"","\"Welcome, life!\""],"why":"She went home with joy."},{"q":"What were Mr Honest's last words?","o":["\"Grace reigns!\"","\"Farewell, night\"","\"Hold out, faith and patience\"","\"Welcome, life\""],"why":"Grace, from start to finish."},{"q":"Complete: \"...commit thou to faithful men, who shall be able to ___ others also.\"","o":["teach","pay","carry","find"],"why":"2 Timothy 2:2. Pass it on!"}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Who stayed behind to guide new pilgrims?","o":["Great-heart","Giant Despair","Madam Bubble","Mr Brisk"],"why":"Leaders keep leading, so others can make it home too."},"choices":[{"title":"Dirt that won't stick","q":"Someone starts spreading lies that you cheated in the exam you worked hard for. People are whispering.","o":[{"t":"Stay calm, keep doing what's right, and let your teacher see the truth.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like the man on Mount Innocent, dirt thrown at a good life won't stick."},{"t":"Spread lies about them too.","f":"That just makes your clothes dirty too."},{"t":"Stop working hard. What's the point?","f":"Well doing is exactly what silences foolish talk (1 Peter 2:15)."}]},{"title":"Three against one","q":"Three friends keep pushing you to drop church and youth group: \"It's boring. Join us on Sundays, or we're done with you.\"","o":[{"t":"Stay kind, but hold your ground, and invite them along.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Valiant-for-truth: no joining, no going back, but no hatred either."},{"t":"Give in so you don't lose them.","f":"Valiant-for-truth wouldn't switch sides, even three to one."},{"t":"Insult them and cut them off.","f":"Hold your sword tight, but use it for truth, not insults."}]},{"title":"The Enchanted Ground","q":"You've started staying up very late on your phone. You're sleepy in class, and you've stopped praying and reading your Bible.","o":[{"t":"Set phone limits, ask a friend to check on you, and restart your quiet time.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Don't sit down in Slothful's Friend. Stay awake, with a partner."},{"t":"It's fine. You'll fix it later.","f":"That's what Heedless and Too-bold thought, and they couldn't wake up."},{"t":"Stop going to school instead.","f":"That's going deeper into the Enchanted Ground."}]},{"title":"Pass on the sword","q":"You've led the school's environmental club for two years. You're about to move to a new school.","o":[{"t":"Train a junior to lead, hand over your notes, and introduce them to the teachers.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! \"My sword I give to him that shall succeed me.\""},{"t":"Just leave. They'll figure it out.","f":"Great leaders don't just finish. They pass it on."},{"t":"Close the club, since you won't be there.","f":"The work should outlive you. That's legacy."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"celestial","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Part II, Chapter 5 in real life."},{"sc":"mountains","n":"🪞 Look in the mirror. Read God's Word every day. It shows you who you are, and who Jesus is."},{"sc":"road","n":"🗡️ Hold your sword tight. Stay constant, come wind, come weather."},{"sc":"enchanted","n":"🧎 Kneel when tempted. Shiny offers pop like bubbles. Pray, and find a partner."},{"sc":"beulah","n":"🕊️ Bless the people coming after you, with your words and your example."},{"sc":"celestial","n":"🎺 Pass on the sword. Train someone to lead after you. That's real leadership."}],"stops":{"p2c5s1":{"story":[{"sc":"mountains","n":"At last the whole group reaches the Delectable Mountains. The Shepherds welcome them, especially the weak ones: Mr Feeble-mind, Mr Ready-to-halt, Mr Despondency and Much-afraid."},{"sc":"mountains","w":"knowledge","e":"smile","t":"Welcome! We always look after the weak ones first. Come in and rest."},{"sc":"mountains","n":"On {Mount Innocent}, they see a man dressed all in white. Two men, Prejudice and Ill-will, keep throwing dirt at him."},{"sc":"mountains","n":"But the dirt won't stick! It falls straight off, and his clothes stay perfectly clean."},{"sc":"mountains","w":"knowledge","e":"smile","t":"When people throw dirt at someone who lives a good life, it won't stick. In the end, the truth shows."},{"sc":"mountains","n":"On {Mount Charity}, they see a man with a big roll of cloth, cutting coats for poor people. He keeps cutting and giving, but the roll never gets smaller!"},{"sc":"mountains","w":"mercy","e":"big","t":"That's like Gaius's riddle! The more he gives, the more he has!"},{"sc":"mountains","n":"In the Shepherds' house, Mercy sees a special mirror. Look one way, and it shows your own face. Look the other way, and it shows the face of the Prince of pilgrims."},{"sc":"mountains","w":"mercy","e":"worried","t":"I'd love that mirror so much. Do you think they'd let me have it?"},{"sc":"mountains","n":"The Shepherds happily give it to her. The mirror is the Word of God: it shows you who you really are, and who Jesus is."}],"quote":{"text":"For if any be a hearer of the word, and not a doer, he is like unto a man beholding his natural face in a glass.","who":"James 1:23","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Live clean, give freely, look in the mirror","text":"Dirt thrown at a good life won't stick forever. Giving never empties a generous heart. And the mirror Mercy loved, the Word of God, shows you yourself honestly, and shows you Jesus. Leaders keep their lives clean, keep giving, and keep looking into the Word."},"think":"If you looked into Mercy's mirror today, what would it show you about yourself?","quiz":[{"q":"Who did the Shepherds look after first?","o":["The weak ones","The strongest","The richest","Great-heart"],"why":"Good shepherds care for the weak first."},{"q":"What happened to the dirt thrown at the man on Mount Innocent?","o":["It fell off. His clothes stayed clean","It covered him","He threw it back","It turned to gold"],"why":"Lies about a good life don't stick forever."},{"q":"What was special about the roll of cloth on Mount Charity?","o":["It never got smaller, however much he gave","It was gold","It was tiny","It was stolen"],"why":"Generosity never runs out."},{"q":"What did Mercy's mirror show?","o":["Her own face, and the face of the Prince","Only her face","The future","Nothing"],"why":"The Word of God shows us ourselves, and shows us Jesus."},{"q":"What does the mirror stand for?","o":["The Word of God","Money","Fame","A phone"],"why":"It shows us the truth about ourselves."}]},"p2c5s2":{"story":[{"sc":"road","n":"Back on the road, they find a man standing with his sword drawn. His face is covered in cuts. His name is {Mr Valiant-for-truth}."},{"sc":"road","w":"greatheart","e":"shock","t":"Friend, what happened to you?"},{"sc":"road","w":"valiant","e":"stern","t":"Three men attacked me: Wild-head, Inconsiderate and Pragmatic. They said, \"Join us, go back home, or die.\""},{"sc":"road","w":"valiant","e":"stern","t":"I told them I wouldn't join them, I wouldn't go back, and I'd fight. We fought for three hours. In the end, they ran."},{"sc":"road","w":"greatheart","e":"smile","t":"Three against one, and you held your ground! Let me see your sword."},{"sc":"road","w":"greatheart","e":"big","t":"Ha! It's a true {Jerusalem blade}! With a sword like this, a man can face an angel. The only trick is to keep hold of it."},{"sc":"road","w":"valiant","e":"smile","t":"I held on so tight, the sword and my hand almost grew together!"},{"sc":"road","n":"Then Valiant-for-truth tells how his family and friends begged him not to become a pilgrim. They said the road was full of lions, giants, swamps and dangers. But he came anyway."},{"sc":"road","w":"valiant","e":"big","t":"Who would true valour see, let him come hither; one here will constant be, come wind, come weather.","b":true},{"sc":"road","w":"valiant","e":"big","t":"There's no discouragement shall make him once relent his first avowed intent to be a pilgrim!"}],"quote":{"text":"Who would true valour see, Let him come hither; One here will constant be, Come wind, come weather.","who":"Valiant"},"lesson":{"title":"Hold your sword tight","text":"Valiant-for-truth was outnumbered three to one, but he didn't give in, go back, or switch sides. His sword, the Word of God, worked because he held onto it so tightly. Leaders who stand for the truth will be tested. Keep hold of God's Word, and stay constant, come wind, come weather."},"think":"Who or what tries to pull you away from what you believe? What helps you hold on?","quiz":[{"q":"How many men attacked Valiant-for-truth?","o":["Three","One","Ten","A hundred"],"why":"Wild-head, Inconsiderate and Pragmatic."},{"q":"What three choices did they give him?","o":["Join us, go back, or die","Pay, run, or hide","Sing, dance, or sleep","Eat, drink, or rest"],"why":"He refused to join them or go back."},{"q":"What kind of sword did he have?","o":["A Jerusalem blade","A wooden sword","A silver sword","A broken sword"],"why":"It stands for the Word of God."},{"q":"What was the secret of using the sword well?","o":["Keeping a tight hold of it","Swinging it fast","Keeping it sharp","Hiding it"],"why":"He held it so tightly his hand nearly grew to it!"},{"q":"Complete: \"One here will constant be, come wind, come ___.\"","o":["weather","night","morning","rain"],"why":"Steady in all conditions."}]},"p2c5s3":{"story":[{"sc":"enchanted","n":"Now they reach the Enchanted Ground, where the air makes people sleepy. Thorns and briars grow over the path, and it's foggy and dark."},{"sc":"enchanted","n":"They pass an arbour with soft cushions. It's called Slothful's Friend. Great-heart doesn't let anyone sit down."},{"sc":"enchanted","w":"greatheart","e":"stern","t":"Keep walking. If you sit down here, you may never get up again."},{"sc":"enchanted","n":"They find two men fast asleep in another arbour: {Heedless} and {Too-bold}. Great-heart shakes them, but they won't wake up. They just mumble in their sleep."},{"sc":"enchanted","w":"greatheart","e":"worried","t":"They started well, but they stopped watching. This is so sad."},{"sc":"enchanted","n":"Then, a bit further on, they see a man kneeling in the road with his hands and eyes lifted up, praying. His name is {Mr Stand-fast}."},{"sc":"enchanted","w":"standfast","e":"smile","t":"Thank God you've come. I was just praying for help."},{"sc":"enchanted","w":"standfast","e":"worried","t":"A woman called {Madam Bubble} came to me. She offered me money, pleasure and an easy life, if I would just follow her."},{"sc":"enchanted","w":"standfast","e":"stern","t":"The more I said no, the more she kept smiling and offering. So I got on my knees and prayed."},{"sc":"enchanted","w":"greatheart","e":"stern","t":"Madam Bubble has pulled many pilgrims off this road. Whatever she offers looks shiny, but it pops like a bubble. You did right to pray."}],"quote":{"text":"Watch and pray, that ye enter not into temptation.","who":"Jesus (Matthew 26:41)","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Stay awake, and kneel when tempted","text":"Heedless and Too-bold started the journey, but fell asleep in a comfortable place and wouldn't wake up. Mr Stand-fast was tempted with money and pleasure, and he got on his knees. Leaders don't get comfortable on the Enchanted Ground. When temptation comes, they pray, and they find friends to walk with."},"think":"What 'Madam Bubble' offers look shiny to young people today? What would help you say no?","quiz":[{"q":"What was the comfortable arbour called?","o":["Slothful's Friend","Pilgrim's Rest","Palace Beautiful","Peace"],"why":"A trap disguised as a resting place."},{"q":"Who were the two sleepers?","o":["Heedless and Too-bold","Simple and Sloth","Faithful and Hopeful","Matthew and James"],"why":"They stopped watching, and couldn't be woken."},{"q":"What was Mr Stand-fast doing when they found him?","o":["Kneeling and praying","Sleeping","Running","Eating"],"why":"He prayed when temptation came."},{"q":"What did Madam Bubble offer?","o":["Money, pleasure and an easy life","A sword","A map","A crown"],"why":"Shiny offers that pop like bubbles."},{"q":"Why is she called Madam Bubble?","o":["What she offers looks shiny, but pops","She blows bubbles","She lives in water","She's round"],"why":"The world's offers don't last."}]},"p2c5s4":{"story":[{"sc":"beulah","n":"At last they reach the land of Beulah. The sun shines day and night. Bells ring from the Celestial City. They wait there, resting, until the King calls them home."},{"sc":"beulah","n":"One day, a messenger arrives with a letter for Christiana. The Master is calling her to come and be with Him in ten days' time."},{"sc":"beulah","w":"christiana","e":"smile","t":"So it's my turn to cross the river. I'm not afraid. I've waited for this day."},{"sc":"beulah","n":"She calls everyone together. She thanks Great-heart for leading them so faithfully."},{"sc":"beulah","w":"christiana","e":"smile","t":"My sons, be good men. Look after your families. Keep walking with God."},{"sc":"beulah","w":"christiana","e":"smile","t":"Mercy, my dear friend. You came along without a letter, and look how God has blessed you!"},{"sc":"beulah","w":"christiana","e":"smile","t":"And to each of you weak ones, Feeble-mind, Ready-to-halt, Despondency, Much-afraid: God has carried you, and He will carry you home."},{"sc":"deepriver","n":"On the day she is called, the road is full of people who have come to watch her go. Christiana walks into the river."},{"sc":"deepriver","w":"christiana","e":"big","t":"I come, Lord, to be with Thee, and bless Thee!","b":true},{"sc":"celestial","n":"On the other side, chariots and horses are waiting. She is carried up to the gate, and the people of the city welcome her in with joy. Christian is waiting for her."},{"sc":"beulah","n":"Her four sons and Mercy stay behind for now. They have families of their own, and a job to do: to help many more people find the road."}],"quote":{"text":"I come, Lord, to be with Thee, and bless Thee.","who":"Christiana"},"lesson":{"title":"Finish well, and bless the next generation","text":"Christiana once mocked the journey. She ended it surrounded by her sons, her friend and the weak pilgrims she cared for. Before she crossed, she blessed each one. Leaders finish well, and they spend their last words building up the people who will carry on after them."},"think":"Who has encouraged you the way Christiana encouraged her family? Have you ever thanked them?","quiz":[{"q":"Where did the pilgrims wait to be called home?","o":["The land of Beulah","Vanity Fair","Doubting Castle","The City of Destruction"],"why":"A sunny land right next to the Celestial City."},{"q":"Who did Christiana thank for leading them?","o":["Great-heart","Giant Despair","Mr Brisk","Demas"],"why":"Their faithful guide all the way."},{"q":"What did Christiana remind Mercy?","o":["She came without a letter, and God blessed her","She should go home","She owed money","She was too slow"],"why":"Remember Stop 2 of Chapter 1? Christiana asked for her at the gate."},{"q":"What did Christiana say as she entered the river?","o":["\"I come, Lord, to be with Thee, and bless Thee!\"","\"Help me!\"","\"Wait for me!\"","\"I'm scared!\""],"why":"She wasn't afraid. She was going home."},{"q":"Why did her sons and Mercy stay behind for now?","o":["To help many more people find the road","They were lost","They didn't want to go","They were sick"],"why":"Leaders leave people behind who will carry on the work."}]},"p2c5s5":{"story":[{"sc":"beulah","n":"Then, one by one, the other pilgrims are called home. Each of them crosses the river in their own way."},{"sc":"deepriver","n":"Mr Ready-to-halt goes first. He leaves his crutches to his son, \"with a hundred warm wishes that he may prove better than I have done.\" Then he steps into the river: \"Welcome, life!\""},{"sc":"deepriver","n":"Mr Feeble-mind is next. As he steps into the water, he says, \"Hold out, faith and patience!\""},{"sc":"deepriver","n":"Mr Despondency and his daughter Much-afraid cross together. \"Farewell, night! Welcome, day!\" he calls. Much-afraid goes through the river singing."},{"sc":"deepriver","n":"Old Mr Honest crosses next. His last words are short and sweet: \"Grace reigns!\""},{"sc":"deepriver","w":"valiant","e":"smile","t":"My sword I give to him that shall succeed me in my pilgrimage, and my courage and skill to him that can get it.","b":true},{"sc":"deepriver","w":"valiant","e":"big","t":"Death, where is thy sting? Grave, where is thy victory?"},{"sc":"celestial","n":"So Mr Valiant-for-truth passes over, and all the trumpets sound for him on the other side."},{"sc":"deepriver","n":"Last is Mr Stand-fast. Halfway across, he stops and speaks to his friends: \"I see myself now at the end of my journey. My toilsome days are ended.\""},{"sc":"celestial","w":"standfast","e":"big","t":"Take me, for I come unto Thee!"},{"sc":"celestial","n":"Great-heart stays behind to guide more pilgrims. And Christiana's sons and their families stay too, to help the church grow and lead many others to the road."},{"sc":"celestial","n":"THE END of The Pilgrim's Progress, Part II. The story that began with one man, alone, asking \"What shall I do?\" ends with a crowd of pilgrims, a family, and leaders ready to guide the next generation."}],"quote":{"text":"My sword I give to him that shall succeed me in my pilgrimage, and my courage and skill to him that can get it.","who":"Valiant"},"lesson":{"title":"Pass on the sword","text":"Valiant-for-truth didn't take his sword with him. He gave it to whoever would come next. Great-heart and Christiana's sons stayed behind to guide new pilgrims. The greatest leaders don't just finish their own journey. They pass on their courage, skills and faith to the next generation."},"think":"Who could you 'pass your sword' to: a younger sibling, a junior at school, a new member at church?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Mr Ready-to-halt do with his crutches?","o":["Left them to his son, with warm wishes","Took them across the river","Gave them to Great-heart","Broke them"],"why":"Even his crutches became a gift to the next generation. \"Welcome, life!\""},{"q":"What were Mr Honest's last words?","o":["\"Grace reigns!\"","\"Goodbye\"","\"Help!\"","\"I'm tired\""],"why":"Short and sweet, just like him."},{"q":"What did Valiant-for-truth do with his sword?","o":["Gave it to whoever would come after him","Took it with him","Threw it in the river","Buried it"],"why":"He passed it on to the next generation."},{"q":"What happened when Valiant-for-truth crossed?","o":["All the trumpets sounded for him","Nothing","It rained","He came back"],"why":"A hero's welcome."},{"q":"Who stayed behind to guide new pilgrims?","o":["Great-heart and Christiana's sons","Giant Despair","Mr Brisk","Nobody"],"why":"Leaders make sure the work continues."}]}}}});
